{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects","id":1373007,"title":"V5: Ashirra and Future Sects?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-05T11:06:14-08:00","id":1373007,"title":"V5: Ashirra and Future Sects?","content":"As someone relatively new to the game and setting, I was wondering what you all thought the likelihood of an Ashirra sourcebook in the future would be. Also, are there any other sects or groups that might be brought into greater prominence (or maybe even restructured into being political sects) that you think are likely to be included in the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:41:34-08:00","id":1373015,"title":"","content":"I really hope so. I like the Ashirra. Veil of Night for Dark Ages has stuff about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:11:13-08:00","id":1373028,"title":"","content":"I quite like the Drowned and the Laibon, too. I think they make the world a lot more interesting and packed with hidden history. I have a cynical suspicion that the franchise's current owners will use them as just an excuse to place limits on the amount of geography they have to cover in order to work with the clans and characters they care about. Beyond this point, there be dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:37:00-08:00","id":1373039,"title":"","content":"I feel the Ashirra is best as Camarilla+. Even if it's older, it would've been something that would've been absorbed into the larger body.<br /> <br /> The Laibon...<br /> Oh boy.<br /> The dual nature thing's really, really cool.<br /> But a pan-african vampire society that's not the Camarilla... Africa doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel the attempt to make the Camarilla a <i>White</i> thing, rather than a global conspiracy, and giving other cultures their just do, is... dishonest. That V5 wants to double down on a problem element. When worldbuilding something that parrallels the real world, you should work out the sociology, logistics, people involved... You don't give serious considerations to whites because you wanna criticise them and then give Africans a Utopian society because africans have gone through a lot and deserve to be propped up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:38:14-08:00","id":1373041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373015#post1373015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope so. I like the Ashirra. Veil of Night for Dark Ages has stuff about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this. I've enjoyed the Ashirra since I first picked up Revised in the back-when times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:00:16-08:00","id":1373049,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Kindred of the Ebony Kingdoms yet. Is it worth buying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:54:55-08:00","id":1373066,"title":"","content":"I hope a Gehenna War book with Ashirra vs Sabbat. The Cults of Blood Cults of Blood Gods of Blood are nearly sects by their own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T14:59:46-08:00","id":1373081,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this is a dumb question, but would it be feasible to introduce/re-flavor Kuei-Jin, Laibon, Drowned Legacies, etc. as regional Kindred conspiracies the same way that the Camarilla deals with the European world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T15:44:13-08:00","id":1373085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373039#post1373039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the Ashirra is best as Camarilla+. Even if it's older, it would've been something that would've been absorbed into the larger body.<br /> <br /> The Laibon...<br /> Oh boy.<br /> The dual nature thing's really, really cool.<br /> But a pan-african vampire society that's not the Camarilla... Africa doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel the attempt to make the Camarilla a <i>White</i> thing, rather than a global conspiracy, and giving other cultures their just do, is... dishonest. That V5 wants to double down on a problem element. When worldbuilding something that parrallels the real world, you should work out the sociology, logistics, people involved... You don't give serious considerations to whites because you wanna criticise them and then give Africans a Utopian society because africans have gone through a lot and deserve to be propped up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't understand this at all. What you makes you think Camarilla is even a &quot;White&quot; thing in the first place? You say it as if other Vampires pulled from other races aren't in the Sect at all. Also I'm Black and I've read Ebony Kingdom, I found no inconsistencies on how the Laibon operate. Why do you make it seem the Laibon can't have a pan-african organization? They aren't even a pan-african conglomerate to begin with anyway, they work as parcelled &quot;Kingdoms&quot; ruled by different Guruhl Methuselah equivalents. Your argument doesn't make sense, because the Laibon Legacies predate the formation of the Camarilla, so why the hell would they be apart of it lol. Laibon society isn't utopian either if you actually bothered to read the Ebony Kingdoms book.<br /> <br /> If I remember daintly the only European Legacy among the Laibon are a bloodline from the <s>Malkavians</s> Toreador(?) (EDIT: Looked it up, they are called the Ishtarri) who are now Berber I believe, other than that Western Kindred didn't really have contact with the Laibon until the Imperial Age. Though I think I remember some Giovanni had some contact before with the slave outposts their merchant kine had on the coasts. Beside that Camarilla has really zero influence supernaturally in sub-sahara Africa. You should really read the classics and try to understand oWoD before recommending things change the mainly disliked &quot;V5&quot; way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-05-2020, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T16:22:45-08:00","id":1373091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373039#post1373039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the Ashirra is best as Camarilla+. Even if it's older, it would've been something that would've been absorbed into the larger body.<br /> <br /> The Laibon...<br /> Oh boy.<br /> The dual nature thing's really, really cool.<br /> But a pan-african vampire society that's not the Camarilla... Africa doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel the attempt to make the Camarilla a <i>White</i> thing, rather than a global conspiracy, and giving other cultures their just do, is... dishonest. That V5 wants to double down on a problem element. When worldbuilding something that parrallels the real world, you should work out the sociology, logistics, people involved... You don't give serious considerations to whites because you wanna criticise them and then give Africans a Utopian society because africans have gone through a lot and deserve to be propped up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth questioning <i>how</i> the Camarilla is a global conspiracy or how it's a white thing as the case may be, using the same techniques as you say. What I assume is that majority of elders in Europe who survived the pretty much all either joined the Camarilla, the Sabbat or went/remained autarkis, with some exceptional enclaves in clans Tzimisce and Giovanni. This was possibly because they were a small community (compared to human nations) under common existential threats. Following that, both sects expanded into new continents that didn't have high populations of native vampire, i.e. the Americas, Australia and presumably New Zealand, basically because vampires originated in western Asia and don't migrate easily. Whereas they didn't have much success settling much of Africa or eastern Asia, which had plenty of their own vampires.<br /> <br /> As I recall, the books (or at least one of them) said that Ashirra sort of merged with the Camarilla some time after the latter was founded. Is it plausible that most native communities of vampires in Asia and Africa were either assimilated or replaced? Or was it global from the start, like the Mage Council of Nine Mystic Traditions*.<br /> <br /> *I'm tempted to refer to the Pentacle Orders of Mage: The Awakening 2E, given how Eurocentric the Traditions are, but even the Orders coalesced in Eurasia and expanded to other mages from there, albeit faster than non-mages established global communications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:28:55-08:00","id":1373132,"title":"","content":"Well to answer your question- Kindred don't exist in Asia and the Laibon were never replaced or assimilated at all by the Camarilla, despite their mortal counterparts being colonized in the 19th through 20th century by the European kine. The only time another group of Vampires were assimilated or replaced, was when European Kindred in the form of the Sabbat fought against the Mesoamerican Vampires when they followed their herds to the Americas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-05-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:48:58-08:00","id":1373134,"title":"","content":"For my own worldbuilding I would probably make it easy in the Modern Nights to just say that the Ashirra and Laibon, or at least their establishments, joined the Camarillas as they both see a value in the Traditions of &quot;Caine&quot;, do not value a conflict with Western Kindred for its own sake, like the idea of cooperation in a more connected world and don't like the Sabbat (the example from Mesoamerica was probably a selling point in that direction) and after joining the Camarilla - unlife continued as before with no change whatsoever except that they have a Camarilla logo on their cards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T20:07:44-08:00","id":1373138,"title":"","content":"Yeah that sounds like a really bad idea. Vampires are really territorial, stubborn, and very long lived. I sincerely doubt the Laibon would ever put much credence in Camarilla philosophy at all. The Camarilla isn't compatible with how the Laibon are with their ruling system. Even in the 21st century well after pre-Imperial uplift to modernity/westernization by the former colonial nations, most Laibon elders have domains FAR in the rural and unmodern parts of Africa still. Not only that I supremely doubt the Guruhl would tolerate their positions to be usurped by an organization mostly ruled by the Venture. They wouldn't have that. Ashirra I don't really know and I don't know if they were even incorporated into the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> When reading the Ebony Kingdom book, they even tell you that while their mortal kine counterparts failed to stave off European colonial wars, the Laibon roughly beat away and kept a stalemate with the Camarilla that followed their Imperial kine for enough years until the Decolonial era. That doesn't surprise me since pre-Industrial sub-sahara Africa was really <b>deadly</b> and short, where rival tribes would raid you to sell you off into slavery, no real medicine beside folk ones, deadly predators around, diseases, etc.<br /> <br /> On top of that through the WoD lens, Laibon have to contend with all the other various Fera Breeds in Africa, that to remind were never killed off in the War of Rage- so they'd probably had to intrigue and fight against deadly killing machines other than wolves. Vampires on their own aren't harmed by bullets that much (a striking reason why the mortal African kine lost so badly in Colonialism), so the Cam at the get go don't have many options. Not only that the Laibon would probably have more sheer fighting experience, because again, its pre-Industrial tribal Africa.<br /> <br /> Making everything Camarilla around the globe just 'cuz doesn't make sense. Their should be more Sects around the globe. This how we get bad ideas where the Sabbat got &quot;removed&quot; in V5. Instead of removing Sects, make more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-05-2020, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T20:22:12-08:00","id":1373143,"title":"","content":"EDITED: My mistake. Forget about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 03-05-2020, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T21:45:38-08:00","id":1373153,"title":"","content":"For my v5 game I'll probably have Cammie and am.narchs in North America. Laibon in Africa. Ashirra in the middle East and North Africa. Drowned in South America. I'll turn the kue jin courts into regular kindred in Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T01:59:16-08:00","id":1373166,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I haven't read KotEk in a while and only read it breifly, and between that time I read about what was going on with changing breeds in africa, which was rediculously optimistic. So yeah I forgot a lot and assumed KotEk fell into the standard trap of &quot;Europe is bad and static, America is bad and new, Australia is hell because of europeans, Asia is superior because it's so-not-european and everyone does yoga and bushido, Africa is a wonderland because IRL they got the short end of the stick and social justice demands they get nice things, Wakanda forever!&quot; <br /> <br /> So yeah, my post might've been far too influenced by the state of Africa in Werewolf:The Apocalypse where, after a failed genocide, everyone happily holds hands with rival changing breeds for the good of the continent. <br /> <br /> But the Ashirra. <br /> Yeah<br /> <br /> They'd be folded into the cam. Their differences with the Cam can easily be a matter of local policies. Unlike Africa, they don't have a huge cultral difference with the europeans and have a strong shared history; Parts of the middle east were pagan, then christian, then the Muslims rose in the latter part of the first millennium; That's not a huge cultural gulf, just a different branch of abrahamic religion. I don't see why middle eastern vampires would be outside of the inner circle. The only big concern here is that I can't really find anything on a Muslim inquisition (A google search does not give desired topics) or a backdrop for an Anarch revolt (But I'm limited to english here so, just because I can't find it, doesn't mean it's not there). There's a lot of little subgroups in Islam, maybe we can point towards conflicts with them. <br /> <br /> Fuck, I'd believe the Cam was really a secular extension of the Ashirra, that's a thought. <br /> <br /> But I find that white people going 'oh, let's double down on the islamic vampire organization to attract middle-eastern players&quot;....<br /> <br /> Yeah, don't do that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T04:06:45-08:00","id":1373173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373166#post1373166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd be folded into the cam.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this mean? Do the Justiciars have authority in the Ashirra? Is Suleiman ibn Abdullah included in the Inner Circle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373166#post1373166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only big concern here is that I can't really find anything on a Muslim inquisition (A google search does not give desired topics) or a backdrop for an Anarch revolt (But I'm limited to english here so, just because I can't find it, doesn't mean it's not there). There's a lot of little subgroups in Islam, maybe we can point towards conflicts with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that the Ashirra/Camarilla model works, they wouldn't have had a Muslim inquisition or an internal War of Princes leading to an Anarch revolt. Maybe similar events were part of the formation of the Ashirra, instigated by its founders. I would expected that to be explained <i>Veil of Night</i>, but I haven't read it.<br /> <br /> And all this makes me wonder how far east the Camarilla and Sabbat originally existed. The Inquisition is associated with the Catholic Church. Did they hunt vampires in Eastern Orthodox countries? Were the clans in Russia concerned with the events? What about the Caucasus? Yerevan is mentioned in the Autarkis section of V5's corebook and is said to have resisted all attempts by the Camarilla to establish a prince or primogen council. Tblisi, in the Anarch book, used to have a medieval Tzimisce elder for a prince, which is unusual for the Camarilla and Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-06-2020, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T04:30:31-08:00","id":1373175,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> thanks for the info about Ebony Kingdoms. I\u2019m defo gonna buy it now.<br /> <br /> Question: is the Nagloper Lineage related to the Tzimisce? (I\u2019m sure the book answers this question, but I don\u2019t want to wait till I buy it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T10:08:36-08:00","id":1373220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373175#post1373175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> thanks for the info about Ebony Kingdoms. I\u2019m defo gonna buy it now.<br /> <br /> Question: is the Nagloper Lineage related to the Tzimisce? (I\u2019m sure the book answers this question, but I don\u2019t want to wait till I buy it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. They are feral Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagloper\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagloper</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T10:24:52-08:00","id":1373225,"title":"","content":"Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T13:23:58-08:00","id":1373247,"title":"","content":"@MyWifeIsScary<br /> <br /> Yeah looks like you didn't really pay attention to W:TA lore when reading the books or even bother to go on the wiki to back your points. Again it has nothing to do with &quot;SJWishism&quot; or &quot;Africa is a wonderland because IRL they got the short end of the stick and social justice demands they get nice things, Wakanda forever!&quot;<br /> <br /> The War of Rage simply didn't happen in Africa and Asia, that's why those continents still have their own various Fera Breeds beside the Wolf variant. It only took place in proto-Europe(?) and nowhere else. Also nothing in Africa is utopian at all, much less through the WoD lens. Don't know why you keep inferring that. This is oWoD, way before the perceived &quot;SJWishisms&quot; gleaned in V5.<br /> <br /> Also again you make it about race when their is no race issue. The Ashirra are an ideological Islamic sect BASED in the Middle-East, so it has nothing to do with &quot;oh, let's double down on the islamic vampire organization to attract middle-eastern players&quot;. If a European Kindred from the Cam became inspired by Islam and wanted to the Ashirra, they could do that. Vice versa for a Middle-East person who was Embraced in the West while knowing nothing of the Ashirra due to being mortal beforehand and just going along with recruitment in the Camarilla or a Middle-East person was born in the West, never even visiting the Middle-East at all so they'll have no obligation or want to join it.<br /> <br /> Also the Ashirra (and their mortal line counterparts) have a HUGE cultural difference/rivalry. Remember the Crusades? The Elders of the Ashirra of the sect definitely remember and we all know Kindred hold huge grudges. Also the fact that you say Middle-East Muslims and secular/maybe Christian at times Europeans don't have big cultural differences is laughable. Just look at the contention in modern France or England with the Muslim minority in those countries. Not only that pretty sure the Ashirra heads don't like how the Camarilla's kine destroyed some of their countries militarily (Iraq and Afghanistan ring a bell? Although WE did have to invade Afghanistan to up lodge the Taliban when they took para-governmental control of the nation, but we've been in there for so long after. Iraq.. &quot;WMDs&quot;... 'Nuff said.)<br /> <br /> So yeah, the notion that the Ashirra and Camarilla would merge is very wishful thinking and just makes for a bad story. Ashirra are /not/ secular at all. The whole point it was made was when a Lasombra(?) Kindred got so inspired by Muhammad's preaching during his prophethood (yes the Sect founder was present when Muhammad was active), that he formed the sect to carry Islam into in unlife as a Vampire as a Road. It's safe to assume that all Ashirra don't go by Humanity in the modern nights at all, but the Islamic Road (forgot the specific name of it). Instead of wiping out more interesting Sects (like what was done with the Sabbat when they all decided to &quot;go to the Middle-East&quot; all at once), conflict between the Islamic Ashirra and the formerly Christian-now-mostly-Secular Camarilla should be explored. Add more, not remove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-06-2020, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:02:52-08:00","id":1373253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373132#post1373132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to answer your question- Kindred don't exist in Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>While everything else you've posted has been Truth, this is not true. There have always been Kindred in Asia from India through Mongolia, Japan, SE Asia and a ( ok, very) few within Mainland China. Its just that they aren't the dominant undead parasite in the region.<br /> <br /> I do think KotEK should have pushed harder to get further away from the European/Middle Eastern Clans as most of the Laibon map pretty much straight onto Camarilla and Sabbat Clans ( ie. Mla Watu = Cappadocians, Shango = Assamites, Akunanse=Gangrel and so on.). I'm a big fan of having somewhere in Africa be the Patient Zero of the Kindred ( Infectious Vampirism), and having that spreading plague be the cause for the fall of older &quot;Vampires&quot; in the regions of Africa, the Middle East, Europe and slowly the rest of the world....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:04:30-08:00","id":1373254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373220#post1373220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it is. They are feral Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagloper\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagloper</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or are the Tzimisce Nagaloper who feign social mores?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T16:08:12-08:00","id":1373277,"title":"","content":"I think your getting things mixed up. Laibon is just the general name for the semi-Sect/Society that comprises sub-sahara Africa. Just like how Western Vampires have the moniker &quot;Kindred&quot;. The Sabbat never had influence in sub-sahara Africa and the Camarilla tried when their mortal kine gained a full foothold during the Colonial era, but failed. The Laibon Legacies (Legacy=Clan) having similar Antediluvian lines as the Western kindred doesn't mean the Sabbat/Camarilla ever had supernatural control, as both of their Antediluvian progenitors superceded the existence of any of these Sects (Sabbat, Camarilla, or Laibon) and the Clans formed after they Embraced the Clan founders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T16:14:22-08:00","id":1373278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373277#post1373277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your getting things mixed up. Laibon is just the general name for the semi-Sect/Society that comprises sub-sahara Africa. Just like how Western Vampires have the moniker &quot;Kindred&quot;. The Sabbat never had influence in sub-sahara Africa and the Camarilla tried when their mortal kine gained a full foothold during the Colonial era, but failed. The Laibon Legacies (Legacy=Clan) having similar Antediluvian lines as the Western kindred doesn't mean the Sabbat/Camarilla ever had supernatural control, as both of their Antediluvian progenitors superceded the existence of any of these Sects (Sabbat, Camarilla, or Laibon) and the Clans formed after they Embraced the Clan founders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ?<br /> <br /> I'm just going to say, Yes you are correct and assume theres some sort of misunderstanding of my post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T01:47:03-08:00","id":1373344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373247#post1373247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MyWifeIsScary<br /> <br /> The War of Rage simply didn't happen in Africa and Asia</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't the Wars of Rage a catch-all term for multiple conflicts? I have an incredibly hard time believing Europeans got bodied by the wolves, Asians didn't, and Africa, not having wolves, just got along. It's not like Werewolves are bad and the rest of the changing breeds are nice, friendly dudes. The only real reason why it's a wolf led-genoicde rather than, say, a Bastet led genoicde, is because the wolves were just better at it. After all, the Asian group wiped out their own bear population, and do you honestly believe Apis and Grondr only existed in Europe? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ashirra are an ideological Islamic sect BASED in the Middle-East, so it has nothing to do with &quot;oh, let's double down on the islamic vampire organization to attract middle-eastern players&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Look, if you need to combat an out of character reason with an in-universe description that supports it.... You're arguing against me, right? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the Ashirra (and their mortal line counterparts) have a HUGE cultural difference/rivalry. Remember the Crusades? </div> </div> </div>Religion was really a backdrop for the crusades. Much of the fighting was very secular, and those in the crusader states learnt to live alongside their counterparts. The crusades were a complicated clusterfuck in a time period where wars were very regular, not a Red VS Blue scenario. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Elders of the Ashirra of the sect definitely remember and we all know Kindred hold huge grudges. Also the fact that you say Middle-East Muslims and secular/maybe Christian at times Europeans don't have big cultural differences is laughable. Just look at the contention in modern France or England with the Muslim minority in those countries </div> </div> </div>I lived in Bradford for a bit, a supposed hotbed, so I know this stuff well. <br /> These problems are<br /> 1- Overstated<br /> 2- Almost entirely the concern of struggling people. Vampires tend not to embrace from the ranks of these very struggling people. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> conflict between the Islamic Ashirra and the formerly Christian-now-mostly-Secular Camarilla should be explored. Add more, not remove. </div> </div> </div>I neither think that wise nor fun. Though i have interest in reinacting the crusades, it better be for good reason. <br /> <br /> Vampires have a top-down view of society. They're analogues of the super rich elites we have today, and these people are predominantly above that shit. <br /> They're happy to create theatre; To rile up the masses against Islam in order to keep the populace devided and ignorant and continue profiteering from misery, but you'll note that a lot of very influentual and rich westerners have great relations with the Saudi Royal family, the US largely created a good chunk of Extremist groups in the middle east, and business is good. <br /> <br /> Nigel Farage champions against immigration, the EU, and against elites who've never worked a good, honest job.<br /> He's an investment banker. Immigrants are convenient, He's against the EU because it threatens UK tax havens, it has some inconvenient regulations, the economic swings are good for currency exchanges and buying up properties while the pound is low, and a divided populace with a right-wing government would be ideal for <s>Vampires</s> I mean rich elites. <br /> Vampires are like nigel, not the masses he sways.<br /> <br /> It would not do well to give rich people (and vampires) poor-people problems. It's not realistic. While you certainly might like the themes of east VS west, it's not right within the context of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i>. And it would really suck for players of the Middle east to have this barrier put up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T04:12:20-08:00","id":1373353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373344#post1373344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and do you honestly believe Apis and Grondr only existed in Europe?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible. Kitsune only exist in Asia, Camazotz and Nuwisha were only in the Americas and the Ajaba are only in Africa (I forget if they're their own breed now or not) so it seems possible the Apis and Grondir were mainly located in Europe.<br /> <br /> Asia did have a War of Shame but it was explicitly different from the War of Rage and the different breeds got back together afterwards. Meanwhile there was never a War of Rage in Africa or the Americas. But at the same time, i's not like the different species got along and everyone was all Kumbaya or anything (look what happened to the Ajaba).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T04:40:20-08:00","id":1373354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1373247#post1373247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's safe to assume that all Ashirra don't go by Humanity in the modern nights at all, but the Islamic Road (forgot the specific name of it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sharia El-Sama it's called in the modern nights, it's detailed in Chaining the Beast. That book does mention there's only a 100 followers left, the youngest of which is 300 years old. So apparently the vast majority of Ashirra are sticking with Humanity. But in the modern nights that makes sense for Masquerade reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 03-07-2020, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T01:22:02-07:00","id":1559269,"title":"","content":"Regarding the original topic, it should be noted that there are many sects within the three Abrahamic religions.. The Prophet \ufdfa<i> said:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Jews split into seventy-one sects, and the Christians split into seventy-two sects, and this [Muslim] community will split into seventy-three sects; all of them will be in the Fire except one.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> You can see here a discussion about the divisions in Islam <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1501266-putting-context-to-the-ahl-i-batin/page3\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...-i-batin/page3</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28917-yahya","name":"Yahya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T05:42:48-07:00","id":1559272,"title":"","content":"To be honest, i treat the Ashirra as just one among several regional inter-court alliances of different reach one can find under the umbrella of the Camarilla (or not) in kindred domains all across the world. &quot;<i>Being in UE or OAS doesn't stop you from belonging to NATO</i>&quot;, so to speak. In fact the Ashirra as i use them are more associated with the Arabian Peninsula proper - closer to their initial portrayal in WoD 2e, in fact - than the rest of the &quot;Arab world&quot;.<br /> <br /> A form of the Laibon definitely exist as some sort of cultural group among the kindred, mostly in sub-saharan Africa though ancillae, elders and even a few princes that count themselves among them might be found in parts of Brazil, the Caribbean, and curiously, Goa and Queensland, Australia.<br /> <br /> That said my take of them is a somewhat inchoate mish-mash of the lineages presented in KotEK, BJD and DAV20 with some changes &amp; twists peppered in. Main reason i have not polished them as much as i'd like is that i'm <b>also </b>retooling the Wan Kuei from KotE (again) and some of the concepts i'm working from (relating to cyclical Gehemna and Thin-Blooded, of all things) will probably be relevant in the African front too.<br /> <br /> They are all kindred so to speak, but at the same time something different and weird to your typical lick coming from a Camarilla-associated city. Though not just the Laibon, Wan Kuei or Gaki, as some &quot;Drowned Legacies&quot; of the Americas are more equal than others and Australia has some weirdness of its own in places, for some examples.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-11-2026, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T03:01:10-07:00","id":1559500,"title":"","content":"Personally I dislike the idea of the Ashirra just being the muslim Camarilla for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> Not in the least it's boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T10:42:13-07:00","id":1559504,"title":"","content":"This was a 7 years old discussion... wtf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Thread necro par excellence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From my POV, the Camarilla is not a Monolith. I have always felt like people overstate how \u201cunified\u201d the Camarilla actually is, especially pre V5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In practice, it is likely much closer to a loose aristocratic network than a centralized organization (similar to northern Italy during the renaissance). Every Prince runs their domain like a personal fiefdom and while there </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>are</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> higher authorities like Justicars and Archons, their influence is not constant.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is only logical, that in your night to night existence as a Kindred, the Prince matters far more than any global Camarilla structure anyway. The Traditions set the framework, but how they\u2019re enforced (and how politics actually plays out) is highly local.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That is why I tend to think of the Camarilla less as a top-down hierarchy and more like something akin to a \u201cmob commission\u201d model: there are powerful figures at the top, but real power is exercised regionally, and the lived experience varies a lot depending on where you are.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now lets look at Ashirra. I do not see them as just a \u201cMuslim Camarilla\u201d either, but as the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>actual</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> dominant power structure in their regions. If you are operating there, that is the system that matters in practice, regardless of any broader claims. Similarly if you are in Capones Chicago, you are still technically in commission territory, but it does not have the exact same rules and structures as lets say NY. Technically same overall system, but in reality different. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So yeah, shared rules, but not shared identity and highly fragmented execution. That tension is kind of the point from my pov.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T04:43:10-07:00","id":1559520,"title":"","content":"That still reflects a pan-national uniformity of political structures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-19-2026, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T12:19:25-07:00","id":1559569,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, there will be some kind of hierarchy. Which is the foil to anarchism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T17:20:50-07:00","id":1559707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1559500#post1559500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I dislike the idea of the Ashirra just being the muslim Camarilla for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> Not in the least it's boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hated the changes they made to the Camarilla from 1st Edition to later ones that the Camarilla went from being a global united alliance of vampires to, &quot;Just Europe and the Americas.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla should be everywhere, insidious, and all powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T09:03:40-07:00","id":1559725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1559707#post1559707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hated the changes they made to the Camarilla from 1st Edition to later ones that the Camarilla went from being a global united alliance of vampires to, &quot;Just Europe and the Americas.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla should be everywhere, insidious, and all powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me that is very very dull and ultimatly wasteful. You have an entire map and all you do is stamp a single way of doing things from norway to nigeria to taiwan. <br /> <br /> One of crappyest pieces of world building i recently saw was a map of asia were all the 'good' countries (capitalist democracies) were anarch and the 'bad' countries (anything else) were carmarilla and as bad as that is, its still more interesting than the carmarilla being a unified world wide power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T19:37:19-07:00","id":1559750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1559725#post1559725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me that is very very dull and ultimatly wasteful. You have an entire map and all you do is stamp a single way of doing things from norway to nigeria to taiwan.<br /> <br /> One of crappyest pieces of world building i recently saw was a map of asia were all the 'good' countries (capitalist democracies) were anarch and the 'bad' countries (anything else) were carmarilla and as bad as that is, its still more interesting than the carmarilla being a unified world wide power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except:<br /> <br /> 1. A unified Camarilla means player characters can visit other domains freely<br /> <br /> 2. It means that there's less disbelief about maintaining the Masquerade<br /> <br /> 3. It means that you can draw from every culture on Earth to make your characters. Want to be an 800 Chinese Legalist in Chicago? Go for it.<br /> <br /> 4. It means that there's a lot more variety in terms of vampires you can theoretically meet as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T23:22:46-07:00","id":1559753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1559750#post1559750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except:<br /> <br /> 1. A unified Camarilla means player characters can visit other domains freely<br /> <br /> 2. It means that there's less disbelief about maintaining the Masquerade<br /> <br /> 3. It means that you can draw from every culture on Earth to make your characters. Want to be an 800 Chinese Legalist in Chicago? Go for it.<br /> <br /> 4. It means that there's a lot more variety in terms of vampires you can theoretically meet as well</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) im not interested in visiting other domains freely,<br /> this is vtm not my 21 something backpacking trip.<br /> <br /> 2) maybe but it also treats masquarade resilance as an asset rather than an obvious conflict point which its supposed to be. Im not keen on hobbitism as a factor in game design.<br /> <br /> 3) you can already do that<br /> <br /> 4) actually theirs less less variety look at 5th and how uniform it is now. Compare classic montreal to modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-04-2026, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T18:06:50-07:00","id":1561668,"title":"","content":"My take:<br /> <br /> - Camarilla: It's an understanding among Princes agreeing about the Primacy of the Traditions, the rules of the Conclave and the few cross-domain institutions, like Justicars and Blood Hunts.<br /> <br /> Kind of ends there. Mostly Princes are left to their own devices. They're also the highest in hierarchy: Justicars have global jurisdiction but not authority, depending on local recognition.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle is the de facto conspiracy, but as such it's not a formal institution. It &quot;doesn't exist&quot;. In lore that is a real but inconsistent depiction, in my games it's true.<br /> <br /> - Ashirra: they don't follow the Traditions, even if common sense makes them follow similar rules. What they follow is Islam, pure and simple. They follow very similar forms of Islam to those practiced by mortals, usually from their mortal days.<br /> <br /> Islam has no concept of intrinsic damnation. A nonhuman intelligent being is as capable as any human of following the Qur'an and reap the same benefits. This is in the book itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;Choosing Islam&quot; today isn't just pragmatism: it is the culture most of them grew within, even a Methuselah today was probably Muslim in life. That said Islam isn't monolithic and the Ashirra has sect interpretations that, while reasonably open, do not encompasses everything.<br /> <br /> The sect's territorial influence isn't the Muslim world or all the Middle East. They're strongest in Saudi Arabia and from there allegiances are always changing, although Afghanistan, Iran and Egypt usually have a number of aligned Sultans.<br /> <br /> While the Camarilla has the Justicars as a sort of international police, the Ashirra has Imams, scholars of religion and law, mostly of law. The real backbone of the sect are the main Imams of each clan, as they determine interpretation of the Shari'a to everyone else. The most influential Imams are from the Banu Haqim, Brujah, Lasombra, Nosferatu and Ventrue clans, and then above even those, the Imam of the Hajj, a small group of Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> - Hecata: a tentative new sect whose backbone are the Necromancer clans. Their goals are the most simple: resist harassment by other sects, help each other in research and make money.<br /> <br /> Their structure is based on family ties, be them by blood or adoption, and a common theme for members is to have a mortal family or group in the know who offers them support.<br /> <br /> Most of other clans and bloodlines who joined are Giovanni family members Embraced out of the Giovanni Bloodline. Sometimes that's the payment for a service, adding new skills to the toolkit, other times it just happens, but family is family and they &quot;rescue&quot; the Childe, appointing a foster sire.<br /> <br /> Adoption into the Hecata does happen, though, either of promising Necromancers or useful assets for the sect. Family unity is mandatory either way. Where other sects focus on general ideas and political structure, the Hecata have a strict demand for loyalty.<br /> <br /> Maybe later I'll continue...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T10:04:08-07:00","id":1561771,"title":"","content":"- The Sabbat: formed in the fires of revolution, united by the Ritae and sharing culture through religion. The Sabbat is complex.<br /> <br /> What defines the Sect is the camaraderie, the pride in being monsters, the war against the Elders, individual freedom and faith. Yet each one of those is simultaneously absolute truth, full of caveats and ultimately kind of false, but not exactly.<br /> <br /> Camaraderie comes from the Vaulderie, but the rite isn't all powerful \u2013 that's kind of the point. Being a monster is good, but what kind of monster is an open question. War isn't suicide, so it's not a constant conflict against anything old, much less their own. Freedom is tempered by all levels of their society, being the most socializing sect. And while some are zealots, faith is a personal matter as long as you publicly espouse the party line and go to the Ritae regularly.<br /> <br /> In practice, the Sabbat is a different beast in each place, in accordance to the individuals there, their own interpretations and their Paths of Enlightenment, or sometimes their Roads. The only constant is the independent Packs and the Auctoritas Ritae.<br /> <br /> - Great Temple of Set: the Followers/Ministry are first and foremost evangelists of their god. Where they arrive, they erect a temple and start to seek converts both mortal and Kindred, and seriously any they can.<br /> <br /> This makes for a curious sect. Sometimes non Kindred get included in a sect for one reason or another. It's rare, but sometimes another bloodsucking creature is included for convenience, or a loyal retainer is revealed to not be a vampire, but still be loyal.<br /> <br /> Followers, though, have diversity in spades. In their temples everyone participate in ceremonies, mortals form the bulk of the Sect, and even their enemies the Serpents dare to invite and try to convert.<br /> <br /> Still, only the true Blood of Set can hold priestly positions, and the vampires of the clan keep command over all those who accept Set as the one to follow (whatever that means to a given group within the faith).<br /> <br /> - Special Cases: those are not Sects. Instead, they're broader groups covering large areas and partially tied by some cultural links, but not actual alliances. True Sects can form within them, though.<br /> -- Laibon: in Africa, specially south of the Sahara, many traits are common to local Vampires, and got intensified by colonial resistance. While white mortals controlled the continent for a long time (and in some senses still do), their institutions here are not under the command of European sects, but the Laibon who expelled the Camarilla and Sabbat with prejudice.<br /> -- Raktasadhus: in India the Vampires follow mortal culture way closer. The Embrace must follow Caste and Jati lines, the origins of vampires are debated in terms of the Hindu god or supernatural tribe who spawned them, and even without an actual sect, the Brahmins keep immense collective influence through religious authority and the magic of Sadhana. It's also the only place where the Ravnos are a local power and the Salubri exist in numbers without abnormal fear. As a curiosity, it's where the city of Golconda is found.<br /> -- The Courts of The Middle Kingdom: while the Kuei-Jin aren't the same species as Kindred, the similar niche puts them in frequent contact where they live. There is no hard and fast rules about what comes from their meetings, but in many cities there is either an alliance between leaders of some factions, or one species is de facto the administration of the area for all the undead.<br /> -- Independent Cities: those are all over the place. No Sect is really capable of keeping control over every city in the world \u2013 there's just not enough vampires \u2013 so when the local ruler decides to not follow any, there's little that can be done in the short term, and some can stay independent a very long time, longer than the current sects existed.<br /> -- Clan Membership is Not a Thing: that must be clear for all Sects. There's no such a thing as a member clan. Few clans have enough central structure to even ponder about the option of establishing a given Sect as mandatory or something, and the sects themselves don't work in this principle. For the Camarilla you're under their law regardless, for the Ashirra they're offering support to any Muslim vampire who accepts, the Setites will receive anyone they can convert. The Sabbat has the acceptance of all as a fundamental policy, and the Giovanni won't deny an opportunity. In the end, they all deal with individuals, not bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T07:08:47-07:00","id":1561894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1561771#post1561771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-- Clan Membership is Not a Thing: that must be clear for all Sects. There's no such a thing as a member clan. Few clans have enough central structure to even ponder about the option of establishing a given Sect as mandatory or something, and the sects themselves don't work in this principle. For the Camarilla you're under their law regardless, for the Ashirra they're offering support to any Muslim vampire who accepts, the Setites will receive anyone they can convert. The Sabbat has the acceptance of all as a fundamental policy, and the Giovanni won't deny an opportunity. In the end, they all deal with individuals, not bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have missed Inconnu, posts invalid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I jest. <br /> <br /> I mostly agree with your take. There is not that much that is universal in Camarilla cities other than Traditions and the upper echelons won't usually get involved with the city unless they are being grossly violated. There are only 7 justicars (well, around that anyway) and even if each of them had 100 archons (preposterous) they would not have time to get involved with every Prince's abuse of power trying to repel Sabbat, curbstomping anarchs, rooting out infernalists and doing other serious shit. Yes, they could get involved at the local level in less serious matters if some big wig pulled the strings (Francois Villon or Kevin Jackson would be likelier to get Justicar or their archons interested in local matters) or if the city is especially important (New York or Vienna definitely count) but that would be the exception rather than the rule. With how big the Camarilla teritorry is and how few Cainites to keep the order Inner Circle is unlikely to send Lucinde to Poznan, Poland because local prince did not give Gangrel a seat on the primogen council in the city. <br /> <br /> But I chose to quote your last bullet point because I so much agree with that. I loved when in Revised WW started to go away from their earlier &quot;7 pillars of Camarilla, 2 of the Sabbat, 4 always independent&quot; stance. In hindsight Gangrel and Brujah being &quot;mainly Camarilla&quot; did not make sense with the broader philosophies and approaches of those clans and Schismatics joining the Camarilla was a great move. But instead of making a nuanced take WW, and Paradox, went to the opposite extreme saying &quot;some clan celebrity said &quot;fuck Camarilla&quot; so most Brujah and Gangrel left the sect&quot;. It doesn't make sense. Yes, some younger vampires would be impressed by the &quot;YOLO&quot; actions of Xaviar and Theo Bell and probably some older vampires with similar outlook on Camarilla would follow in their footsteps but there is no way Brujah and Gangrel in power would en masse leaver their comfy seats of power just because a rebellious archon or even Justicar got fed up with the sect.<br /> <br /> My $0.02 anyway. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T13:21:22-07:00","id":1561910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1561894#post1561894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have missed Inconnu, posts invalid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I jest.<br /> <br /> I mostly agree with your take. There is not that much that is universal in Camarilla cities other than Traditions and the upper echelons won't usually get involved with the city unless they are being grossly violated. There are only 7 justicars (well, around that anyway) and even if each of them had 100 archons (preposterous) they would not have time to get involved with every Prince's abuse of power trying to repel Sabbat, curbstomping anarchs, rooting out infernalists and doing other serious shit. Yes, they could get involved at the local level in less serious matters if some big wig pulled the strings (Francois Villon or Kevin Jackson would be likelier to get Justicar or their archons interested in local matters) or if the city is especially important (New York or Vienna definitely count) but that would be the exception rather than the rule. With how big the Camarilla teritorry is and how few Cainites to keep the order Inner Circle is unlikely to send Lucinde to Poznan, Poland because local prince did not give Gangrel a seat on the primogen council in the city.<br /> <br /> But I chose to quote your last bullet point because I so much agree with that. I loved when in Revised WW started to go away from their earlier &quot;7 pillars of Camarilla, 2 of the Sabbat, 4 always independent&quot; stance. In hindsight Gangrel and Brujah being &quot;mainly Camarilla&quot; did not make sense with the broader philosophies and approaches of those clans and Schismatics joining the Camarilla was a great move. But instead of making a nuanced take WW, and Paradox, went to the opposite extreme saying &quot;some clan celebrity said &quot;fuck Camarilla&quot; so most Brujah and Gangrel left the sect&quot;. It doesn't make sense. Yes, some younger vampires would be impressed by the &quot;YOLO&quot; actions of Xaviar and Theo Bell and probably some older vampires with similar outlook on Camarilla would follow in their footsteps but there is no way Brujah and Gangrel in power would en masse leaver their comfy seats of power just because a rebellious archon or even Justicar got fed up with the sect.<br /> <br /> My $0.02 anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. At most I'd say I prefer the original, very early depiction where Primogen are not an institution, but a substitute to a Prince when no Elder has enough power above the others to do it alone.<br /> <br /> - Inconnu: they're a mystery for many, but truth is that this is not one group. The most known Inconnu are a loose federation of Autarkis that seek Golconda and more or less follow a cabal of Methuselah living in some secret hideout. It is Hunedoara Castle, but that fact is not terribly important.<br /> <br /> Even &quot;follow&quot; is a strong word. The 12 Autarkis are influential due to age and wisdom, despite their failings, but from the actual Inconnu their position mostly boils down to being informed of news around the world. They're powerful and have a number of indirect agents around the place, but ultimately they're also trapped and, despite not being nice, are all quite decent as far as Methuselah go. Their goal is indeed played straight, if not graciously.<br /> <br /> But this also means they don't control the word &quot;Inconnu&quot; and don't try to. Since they're hidden and secretive, most people think anyone who goes Autarkis to seek Golconda is Inconnu and this isn't formally false, so not all Inconnu are part of an Inconnu organization, or the same Inconnu organization.<br /> <br /> In fact, since they're a mystery, not everyone who call themselves Inconnu are Golconda seekers, and they don't have less claim to the name than anyone else, so really: Inconnu is whomever wanna call themselves Inconnu, and the only requirement to be taken seriously at that is to be weird, wander around and seem to be Autarkis. Talking about Golconda optional, but recommended.<br /> <br /> All that said, given their power and proficiency at coordinating global operations from fucking nowhere, the 12 at Hunedoara will likely know and keep tabs about anyone that identifies as Inconnu, spying on them. Not interfere, in most cases, but they know and don't necessarily like what they know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T16:07:55-07:00","id":1561914,"title":"","content":"Monteparnas\u2019 descriptions above remind me of something I\u2019ve been thinking about lately re: vampire, that being that most clans make more sense as cults (with or without unique forms of sorcery) than as \u2018clans\u2019 tbh. Now of course this is the same take as Requiem more or less and I still like the Masq clans and think that 9/10 times it would be too onerous to redefine them, even if it is something I entertain for fun.<br /> <br /> Like, IMO, the clans that make the most sense as actual clans are the Brujah, Gangrel, Nosferatu, Toreador, Ventrue, and maybe the Ravnos (although I think making them a bloodline would also be fine tbh). That being said I don\u2019t think making all the others cults is a perfect solution either - I think Malkavians make more sense as a condition (I\u2019ve always liked the idea of Dementation as a psychic virus) and the Old Clan Tzimisce can easily work as a sub-culture of the Ventrue IMO.<br /> <br /> Then what do we have looking at the rest?<br /> <br /> An organization of hermetic mages who used magick to become vampires (Tremere), a group of vampires who have gained supernatural powers through some form of communion with a force/principle of cthonic darkness (Lasombra), a group who have done the same with a mysterious flesh-warping demonic virus - possibly spread via the vinniculum (Tzimisce), a group of diablerie-cultists dedicated to enforcing a vampiric legal code established by its founder (Assamites), death/necromancy cultists of one stripe or another (Cappadocians/Giovanni/Hecate/etc.), followers of a Gnostic anti-nomian sect with a heart-snake themed unique sorcery (Settites), and followers of an enlightenment-seeker Golconda-teaching visionary (Salubri).<br /> <br /> Of those I think you could divide the above into two camps: A. Those who are part of formal and coherent organizations which can function virtually as micro-sects (Tremere, Assamites, Temple of Set, Giovanni/Hecate*); B. Those which make more sense as vampiric lineages descended from a Founder who carried out a transformative occult ritual and those who have been since inducted (Lasombra, V!Tzimisce, Cappadocians, True Settites, Salubri; plus groups like the Baali).<br /> <br /> Added disambiguation: if you wanted to use this framework I do think the Death Clan and the Settites make somewhat muddled cases. The classic Giovanni and the V5 Hecate are essentially organized conspiracies/micro-sects while also simultaneously (under this framework) being members of a lineage created through the line-founder Cappadocious\u2019 transformative Death ritual. See also the Settites, where the Church of Set can function as a micro-sect which can incorporate any vampiric initiates while being spearheaded by those of the lineage founded by Sutekh.<br /> <br /> Using this Founding system idea, I also think it would make sense that sufficiently powerful sorcerers within these lineages should be able to induct members: whether that\u2019s a heart-removal rite to become a True Settite or being Consecrated in the Abyss to become an obtenebration-gifted Lasombra.<br /> <br /> I also think that if used many of these founded-lineages would not date back into hoary antiquity like clans currently do. For example whether the Assamites can arise prior to Islam is up for debate (I can see an argument for going back to Hammurabi and other bronze-age law givers), I can\u2019t really see the Settites emerging prior to the emergence of Gnosticism in the Mediterranean world-system of the Axial-age or the Salubri emerging prior to the advent of Buddhism in South Asia (or the practice of Yogism in axial age South Asia at the earliest).<br /> <br /> (Admittedly this is somewhat far afield from the OG question of V5 but it seemed in line with the discussion of sects in general and I felt like sharing this concept I was spitballing with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T01:29:06-07:00","id":1561921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1561914#post1561914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monteparnas\u2019 descriptions above remind me of something I\u2019ve been thinking about lately re: vampire, that being that most clans make more sense as cults (with or without unique forms of sorcery) than as \u2018clans\u2019 tbh. Now of course this is the same take as Requiem more or less and I still like the Masq clans and think that 9/10 times it would be too onerous to redefine them, even if it is something I entertain for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should remind because it's mostly the same concept. I completely agree, specially when a given clan has a too strong internal culture as if the members weren't actually mostly random adults taken from their previous life against their will.<br /> <br /> What I think that can balance this a little is two important things: first that the setting follows already a trope of true origins for philosophies and concepts that predate their public version, where most human thought is a later imitation or refinement of the Hidden Cultures. Second that an organization can, in fact, start with a lineage, a founder that did intend not just to establish their culture, but to tie their bloodline to it. This happens IRL after all.<br /> <br /> That's particularly important because the game has a strong theme of blood inheritance: some of your identity is unavoidably defined by your actual ancestry. Not as a sign that blood is the main factor, but that it will haunt you. So I'm not against most of those clans working as both things: there's the culture/group and there is the lineage of the Founder, this last one carry marks of their origin no matter where they go.<br /> <br /> As for the Banu Haqim, the Ashirra basically formalized this already, the sect is pretty much the clan written as a common cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T03:24:08-07:00","id":1561965,"title":"","content":"I tend to treat clans as demographic and cultural trends in terms of politics. Clan ventrue are de facto carmarilla because the clans numbers are largest their which makes sense idealogically and culturally. A sect in turn will declair a clan part of a sect for clout and realpolitik.<br /> at the same time deviance can occur. I always liked the revised attitude to sabbat vampires were their clan id was articulated and framed in the context of the sect via antitribu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-20-2026, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T08:31:43-07:00","id":1561991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1561914#post1561914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monteparnas\u2019 descriptions above remind me of something I\u2019ve been thinking about lately re: vampire, that being that most clans make more sense as cults (with or without unique forms of sorcery) than as \u2018clans\u2019 tbh. Now of course this is the same take as Requiem more or less and I still like the Masq clans and think that 9/10 times it would be too onerous to redefine them, even if it is something I entertain for fun.<br /> <br /> Like, IMO, the clans that make the most sense as actual clans are the Brujah, Gangrel, Nosferatu, Toreador, Ventrue, and maybe the Ravnos (although I think making them a bloodline would also be fine tbh). That being said I don\u2019t think making all the others cults is a perfect solution either - I think Malkavians make more sense as a condition (I\u2019ve always liked the idea of Dementation as a psychic virus) and the Old Clan Tzimisce can easily work as a sub-culture of the Ventrue IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me of a Chronicle idea I never had a chance to run where PCs discover some ancient text proving that clans as vampire knows them are basically a lie (and so most of the Noddist lore). In the First City clans were just vampiric guilds: Assamites were judges, Ventrue leaders, Tzimisce shamas, Brujah were scholars, Salubri were healers and so on. <br /> <br /> Think it would be cool idea and the upheaval where not only Sabbat's ideology is uprooted but also basically pillar of the whole vampiric community could be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T08:40:38-07:00","id":1561992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1561910#post1561910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. At most I'd say I prefer the original, very early depiction where Primogen are not an institution, but a substitute to a Prince when no Elder has enough power above the others to do it alone.<br /> <br /> - Inconnu: they're a mystery for many, but truth is that this is not one group. The most known Inconnu are a loose federation of Autarkis that seek Golconda and more or less follow a cabal of Methuselah living in some secret hideout. It is Hunedoara Castle, but that fact is not terribly important.<br /> <br /> Even &quot;follow&quot; is a strong word. The 12 Autarkis are influential due to age and wisdom, despite their failings, but from the actual Inconnu their position mostly boils down to being informed of news around the world. They're powerful and have a number of indirect agents around the place, but ultimately they're also trapped and, despite not being nice, are all quite decent as far as Methuselah go. Their goal is indeed played straight, if not graciously.<br /> <br /> But this also means they don't control the word &quot;Inconnu&quot; and don't try to. Since they're hidden and secretive, most people think anyone who goes Autarkis to seek Golconda is Inconnu and this isn't formally false, so not all Inconnu are part of an Inconnu organization, or the same Inconnu organization.<br /> <br /> In fact, since they're a mystery, not everyone who call themselves Inconnu are Golconda seekers, and they don't have less claim to the name than anyone else, so really: Inconnu is whomever wanna call themselves Inconnu, and the only requirement to be taken seriously at that is to be weird, wander around and seem to be Autarkis. Talking about Golconda optional, but recommended.<br /> <br /> All that said, given their power and proficiency at coordinating global operations from fucking nowhere, the 12 at Hunedoara will likely know and keep tabs about anyone that identifies as Inconnu, spying on them. Not interfere, in most cases, but they know and don't necessarily like what they know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inconnu are one of the aspects I am most at odds with the canon. The whole Golconda Seekers Unlimited is not my cup of tee. So I just stick to what was written in the original Vampire: the Dark Ages rulebook: Inconnu are some ancient survivors from Rome. They are a loose alliance of Eternal Senate remanants: some want to build new Eternal City, some want to take revenge on those who orchestrated the fall of the Roman Empire and some might even want to hide from the Jyhad and be Autarkis seeking Golconda. So like Tal'Mahe'Ra they would be peppered across different sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T09:18:14-07:00","id":1561994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1561992#post1561992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inconnu are one of the aspects I am most at odds with the canon. The whole Golconda Seekers Unlimited is not my cup of tee. So I just stick to what was written in the original Vampire: the Dark Ages rulebook: Inconnu are some ancient survivors from Rome. They are a loose alliance of Eternal Senate remanants: some want to build new Eternal City, some want to take revenge on those who orchestrated the fall of the Roman Empire and some might even want to hide from the Jyhad and be Autarkis seeking Golconda. So like Tal'Mahe'Ra they would be peppered across different sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're perfectly in line with canon.<br /> <br /> At no point the Inconnu was &quot;Golconda Seekers Unlimited&quot;. They're a <i>mystery</i> known only by that <i>presentation</i>.<br /> <br /> No one knows who they are. Not all their steps are followed. They're not talking about themselves. A weirdo that seems powerful and very secure arrives, wanders around meeting people, gives a public spiel about Golconda and goes away. There's not even any evidence that they really belong to the same group.<br /> <br /> Later lore stays at that: more than one group of Methuselah call themselves Inconnu, don't care about others using the name, and at least some if they people doing so are loners with no idea there are organized groups using it.<br /> <br /> It just so happens that one such group is the real deal, though not all that successful: no one at Hunedoara is even close to Golconda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T18:12:55-07:00","id":1562018,"title":"","content":"I mentioned it before but I think that the Innconu can work as a loose collection of methsulaths that trying to transcend the limits of their existence but it doesn't mean that they are kind and compassionate beings and maybe are willing to commit horrible things to get results and some might be using the name as means to seem more dangerous then they really are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T18:22:31-07:00","id":1562020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DifferentJustin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects#post1373007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone relatively new to the game and setting, I was wondering what you all thought the likelihood of an Ashirra sourcebook in the future would be. Also, are there any other sects or groups that might be brought into greater prominence (or maybe even restructured into being political sects) that you think are likely to be included in the future?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is unlikely because V5 was very much trying to make a more global Camarilla by merging the Ashirra and Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T22:38:14-07:00","id":1562025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562018#post1562018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned it before but I think that the Innconu can work as a loose collection of methsulaths that trying to transcend the limits of their existence but it doesn't mean that they are kind and compassionate beings and maybe are willing to commit horrible things to get results and some might be using the name as means to seem more dangerous then they really are.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already confirmed since Revised at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562020#post1562020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take is unlikely because V5 was very much trying to make a more global Camarilla by merging the Ashirra and Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The merging is irrelevant, they partially backed down anyway.<br /> <br /> It's an alliance, not a merging, but its function is to not have to touch the Ashirra one way or another.<br /> <br /> Paradox won't write about the sect that checks out almost all their Corporate PR Risk boxes, it would require actual careful engaging with the Middle East, culture, history, religion and politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T00:34:30-07:00","id":1562033,"title":"","content":"Good to know Montparnasse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T01:42:05-07:00","id":1562036,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that if someone wanted more cross-sect play, you could also reintroduce the Nephtali from <i>Gehenna</i>: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephtali\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephtali</a> Basically, Pieterzoon sets up a new sect that aims to prevent Gehenna and count Camarilla lies. A fair few Sabbat and independents join. In <i>Gehenna</i>, it's a public organisation that even the mortals know about.<br /> <br /> In a V5-type setting, you can tone that down and make it an alliance between the major sects and independents, perhaps formed in response to the Second Inquisition, to prevent Gehenna and protect Cainites from mortal hunters. A kind of vampire &quot;UN&quot; that allows the sect's to coexist albeit with tension (much like the real UN).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, in a more V20-esque setting, it could be a conspiracy, like a more benign Tal'mahe'Ra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T01:54:47-07:00","id":1562037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562025#post1562025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merging is irrelevant, they partially backed down anyway.<br /> <br /> It's an alliance, not a merging, but its function is to not have to touch the Ashirra one way or another.<br /> <br /> Paradox won't write about the sect that checks out almost all their Corporate PR Risk boxes, it would require actual careful engaging with the Middle East, culture, history, religion and politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, they've just wanted to simplify the setting as much as humanly possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T09:11:17-07:00","id":1562049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562036#post1562036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that if someone wanted more cross-sect play, you could also reintroduce the Nephtali from <i>Gehenna</i>: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephtali\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephtali</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I think they can be played mostly straight if you go with slightly more emphasis on &quot;Gehenna is happening&quot;, which is standard V5 anyway and still possible within V20.<br /> <br /> Switch going public to going as close to it as possible among the supernatural. It may count among members hunters and other entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562037#post1562037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, they've just wanted to simplify the setting as much as humanly possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be na\u00efve, there were many better ways to simplify the setting and no need to even touch on the subject if it was just that.<br /> <br /> That was pure corporate risk management. To ignore the Ashirra is a risk, to engage it is also a risk. Old White Wolf embraced risk and that's why people from minorities love WoD despite so many blunders. But Paradox follows standard PR practices and try to not offend anyone, even if that means pretending they don't exist.<br /> <br /> Making a peace treaty is their perfect compromise. The Ashirra is acknowledged, but won't ever require being cited again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T11:41:53-07:00","id":1562053,"title":"","content":"I would love to see an Ashirra sourcebook for the new 6e system expected to be announced at GenCon, and I think there\u2019s a decent chance it might happen. I also hope to see a book on the Inconnu, keeping in mind that the Inconnu are less a tightly organized sect and more a loose umbrella organization of Kindred sharing a common name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T18:45:22-07:00","id":1562068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562049#post1562049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be na\u00efve, there were many better ways to simplify the setting and no need to even touch on the subject if it was just that.<br /> <br /> That was pure corporate risk management. To ignore the Ashirra is a risk, to engage it is also a risk. Old White Wolf embraced risk and that's why people from minorities love WoD despite so many blunders. But Paradox follows standard PR practices and try to not offend anyone, even if that means pretending they don't exist.<br /> <br /> Making a peace treaty is their perfect compromise. The Ashirra is acknowledged, but won't ever require being cited again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel they managed it in the slightest since the Camarilla book on the Middle East is deeply orientalist and treats the Middle East as one gigantic war zone for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Also a place so mysterious and bloody that all the Elders can go there and fight Dragonball Z style with no one apparently noticing.<br /> <br /> I feel it is MUCH worse off than the previous editions.<br /> <br /> By contrast, wiping out the Kuei Jin via soft retcon was absolutely corporate butt covering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T19:02:08-07:00","id":1562069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1373007-v5-ashirra-and-future-sects?p=1562068#post1562068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel they managed it in the slightest</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, but that's incompetence, not risk taking.<br /> <br /> Also, Gehenna War and the marriage plot are from different moments, they're years apart, so they're not bound to follow the same strategy.<br /> <br /> Especially since they're not even by the same company. The marriage was from Paradox in its most interventionist time over the setting, while Gehenna War is Renegade Studios, and they're blundering all over the place with those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}